    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-csharp

    \title Preview and profile Qt Bridge for C# applications

    You can \l {Preview Qt Quick applications}{preview} and
    \l {Profile QML code}{profile} the QML code of \l {Qt Bridge for C#}
    applications in the same way as other Qt Quick applications. \QVSC starts
    your C# application for you.

    \section1 Build first

    QML Preview and \QP need the metadata that building the project
    generates. Build the project once before you start them. For more
    information, see
    \l {vscodeext-how-to-build-csharp.html}
    {Build and run Qt Bridge for C# applications}.

    If you start them before the first build, \QVSC asks you to build the
    project first.

    \section1 Preview QML files

    To preview the QML file that is open in the editor:

    \list
        \li Select \inlineimage {preview-file.png} {Preview current QML file live}
            on the editor toolbar.
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
            \uicontrol {Qt: Preview current QML file live}.
    \endlist

    The changes you make to the QML code become visible in the preview when
    you save the file. This applies to all QML files of the project, and the
    preview always starts with the saved QML code, so you do not need to
    build the project after changing QML code. Changes to the C# code and
    new QML files take effect after you build the project again.

    \section1 Profile the application

    To profile the application, go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
    \uicontrol {Qt: Profile QML application}.

    \section1 Work with several projects

    If a workspace folder contains several Qt Bridge for C# projects, \QVSC
    uses the project that contains the file in the editor. If that does not
    identify a project, it asks you to select one.

    \section1 Select the build configuration

    If you build a project in several configurations, such as \c Debug and
    \c Release, or for several target frameworks, the project has QML metadata
    for each of them. \QVSC asks you which one to use.

    To select a different build later:

    \list 1
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and select
            \uicontrol {Qt Bridge C#: Select QML Build Metadata}.
        \li Select the configuration and target framework.
    \endlist

    The QML language server, QML Preview, and \QP use the selected build. \QVSC
    remembers the selection for the workspace.

    \sa {vscodeext-how-to-select-qt-csharp.html}
        {Select Qt for Qt Bridge for C# projects}
*/
